# Windows batch scripts MUST be checked out with CRLF.
#
# cmd.exe locates a `call :label` / `goto :label` by seeking in the file, and on
# an LF-only .cmd that seek drifts once the file is a few KB long: the parser
# resumes mid-line and starts executing fragments. publish-js.cmd (11 KB) failed
# with "The system cannot find the batch label specified - publish" for exactly
# this reason — the byte-identical CRLF copy runs clean.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Shell scripts and the Maven wrapper stay LF even on a Windows checkout —
# a CRLF shebang line breaks them under bash/sh.
*.sh text eol=lf
mvnw text eol=lf
